{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Hark, the glad [D7]sound! The [Em]Sa[D]vior [G]comes,
[G]The [D]Sa__[Bm]__[A7]vior [D]pro[A7]mised [D]long!
[D]Let [G]ev[D7]ery heart prepare [G]a [C]throne,
[C]And ev__[D7]__[Em]ery [Am]voice [D7]a [G]song.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]On Him the [D7]Spirit, [Em]large[D]ly [G]poured,
[G]Ex[D]erts__[Bm]__ [A7]its [D]sac[A7]red [D]fire;
[D]Wis[G]dom [D7]and might, and zeal [G]and [C]love,
[C]His ho__[D7]__[Em]ly [Am]breast [D7]in[G]spire.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]He comes the [D7]prisoners [Em]to [D]re[G]lease,
[G]In [D]Sa__[Bm]__[A7]tan’s [D]bon[A7]dage [D]held;
[D]The [G]gates [D7]of brass before [G]Him [C]burst,
[C]The ir__[D7]__[Em]on [Am]fet[D7]ters [G]yield.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]He comes from [D7]thickest [Em]films [D]of [G]vice
[G]To [D]clear__[Bm]__ [A7]the [D]men[A7]tal [D]ray,
[D]And [G]on [D7]the eye-balls of [G]the [C]blind
[C]To pour__[D7]__ [Em]ce[Am]les[D7]tial [G]day. *
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]He comes the [D7]broken [Em]heart [D]to [G]bind,
[G]The [D]bleed__[Bm]__[A7]ing [D]soul [A7]to [D]cure;
[D]And [G]with [D7]the treasures of [G]His [C]grace
[C]T'enrich__[D7]__ [Em]the [Am]hum[D7]ble [G]poor.
{end_of_verse}
